{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vkm8fSuyEANmUKrANQnC4y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"status\": \"ready\",\n3\t  \"summary\": \"Three paragraph-specific gaps justify a small retrieval pass: width-aware parametrization theory, direct prior work on how grokking depends on model width/scale, and statistical methodology for the cluster bootstrap and censored-delay analysis.\",\n4\t  \"missing_literatures\": [\n5\t    \"width-aware parametrization and hyperparameter transfer under Adam (muP / Tensor Programs)\",\n6\t    \"empirical studies of how grokking time depends on model width, size, or weight decay\",\n7\t    \"cluster bootstrap and right-censored (survival / Tobit) regression\"\n8\t  ],\n9\t  \"rewrite_targets\": [\n10\t    {\n11\t      \"target_id\": \"related-work-parametrization\",\n12\t      \"section\": \"related work\",\n13\t      \"priority\": \"high\",\n14\t      \"citation_intent\": \"background\",\n15\t      \"reason\": \"The evaluated model's central design element is a width-dependent multiplier meant to equalize the effective step size under Adam-type updates, and the Discussion argues this could mask or create a width slope. The paragraph supports this only with a reinforcement-learning normalization paper and a dynamical-richness measurement paper; the standard width-aware parametrization literature that motivates exactly this construction is not cited.\",\n16\t      \"anchor_text\": \"Parametrization and optimizer scale: ... width-dependent multipliers on hidden and output layers\",\n17\t      \"search_topics\": [\n18\t        \"maximal update parametrization feature learning in infinite-width networks\",\n19\t        \"hyperparameter transfer across width (muP, Tensor Programs V)\",\n20\t        \"Adam learning-rate scaling with width / parametrization-dependent effective step size\"\n21\t      ]\n22\t    },\n23\t    {\n24\t      \"target_id\": \"intro-related-width-dependence-prior-work\"