{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwJA1LNNRKLLNyVwCtGb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TtWwCxjLRhHmAx8NGQ1P3K","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nplan = {\n \"status\": \"ready\",\n \"central_topic\": \"Post-draft citation gaps for a study of how grokking delay on modular addition depends on transformer width: width-aware (muP-style) parametrization and Adam effective step size, prior empirical grokking work on weight decay, training fraction and initialization scale, and statistical methodology for the seed-cluster bootstrap and right-censored delays.\",\n \"core_methods\": [\n  \"cluster (seed-level) percentile bootstrap with few clusters\",\n  \"right-censored outcome regression (Tobit / accelerated failure time) versus imputing the cap\"\n ],\n \"comparators\": [\n  \"prior empirical grokking studies varying weight decay, training fraction, or initialization scale\"\n ],\n \"benchmarks\": [],\n \"architectural_shifts\": [\n  \"width-dependent multipliers on hidden and output layers (muP-like parametrization) to equalize effective step size under Adam\"\n ],\n \"result_driven_themes\": [\n  \"width slope on log-delay not distinguishable from zero with 40% of runs censored, so censoring handling and parametrization-induced effective-step-size confounds need methodological support\"\n ],\n \"queries\": [\n  {\n   \"query\": \"maximal update parametrization feature learning infinite-width neural networks Tensor Programs\",\n   \"category\": \"architectural_shift\",\n   \"rationale\": \"Gap related-work-parametrization (high): the width-dependent multipliers on hidden and output layers are the muP construction, which the Related Work paragraph on parametrization currently does not cite.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"query\": \"hyperparameter transfer across width zero-shot tuning Adam learning rate scaling parametrization\",\n   \"category\": \"architectural_shift\",\n   \"rationale\": \"Gap related-work-parametrization (high): supports the Discussion claim that width-dependent multipliers equalize effective step size under Adam and could mask or create a width slope.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"query\": \"grokking weight decay training data fraction time to generalization modular arithmetic\",\n   \"category\": \"baseline_comparator\",\n   \"rationale\": \"Gap intro-related-width-dependence-prior-work (high): positions the paper against earlier empirical grokking studies that varied weight decay and training fraction, needed for the Relation to this work paragraph and the capacity-based reading. Phrased around weight decay and data fraction rather than width or model size to follow the forbidden-pattern constraint.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"query\": \"grokking initialization scale effective learning rate weight norm delayed generalization\",\n   \"category\": \"baseline_comparator\",\n   \"rationale\": \"Gap intro-related-width-dependence-prior-work (high): covers initialization-scale and effective-learning-rate dependence of grokking onset, directly relevant to the init-scale and reparametrization confound.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"query\": \"cluster bootstrap inference with few clusters percentile confidence intervals\",\n   \"category\": \"core_method\",\n   \"rationale\": \"Gap method-statistics-cluster-bootstrap-censoring (medium): supports the seed-cluster percentile bootstrap used as the test statistic, including its small-cluster behavior.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"query\": \"regression with right-censored outcomes Tobit accelerated failure time bias of imputing censored values\",\n   \"category\": \"core_method\",\n   \"rationale\": \"Gap method-statistics-cluster-bootstrap-censoring (medium): supports both the critique of entering censored delays at the cap and the Discussion recommendation to analyze delays as censored data.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"forbidden_query_patterns\": [\n  \"generic 'optimization', 'benchmarking', 'scientific method', 'pa